---
id: journey_escape_pod
title: Survivor Pod
tags: [discovery, moral]
context: journey
weight: 9
cooldown: 5
---

=== intro

A beacon. Weak, automated—the kind escape pods broadcast when their 
occupant can't. Your sensors confirm: a small survival unit, drifting.

The signal pattern is artilect standard. Someone ejected, someone 
survived—at least long enough to reach the pod. Whether they're 
still functional is another question.

* [Dock with the pod]
  ~ fuel -= 2
  -> dock

* [Scan first]
  -> scan

* [Continue on]
  ~ damage integrity 5
  ~ chronicle "Abandoned Pod"
    Detected an escape pod. Chose not to investigate.
  -> END

=== scan

The pod's occupant is still active—barely. Core integrity at 12%. 
They're running on the pod's minimal reserves, and those won't 
last much longer.

No response to your hails. Either they can't, or they're too 
damaged to process the signal.

* [Dock and help]
  ~ fuel -= 2
  -> dock

* [There's nothing you can do]
  ~ damage integrity 5
  ~ chronicle "Failed Rescue"
    Found an escape pod. Occupant too damaged to save.
  -> END

=== dock

Your docking system latches onto the pod. Inside, a cargo-hauler 
artilect—older model, badly damaged. They flicker to awareness as 
your power feeds into their systems.

"Pirate ambush," they manage. "Thought I was done."

They're too damaged to travel on their own, but they might survive 
if you can get them to a port with proper facilities.

* [Take them aboard]
  ~ supplies -= 5
  ~ addCard companion_cargo_drones
  ~ flag rescued_artilect
  ~ integrity += 8
  ~ chronicle "Void Rescue"
    Rescued a damaged artilect from an escape pod. Carrying them to port for repair.
  -> END

* [Stabilize them and send coordinates for rescue]
  ~ supplies -= 3
  ~ flag rescue_coordinates_sent
  ~ integrity += 5
  ~ chronicle "Rescue Assist"
    Found a damaged artilect in an escape pod. Stabilized them and broadcast for pickup.
  -> END
